cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use MumaxVR in academic work, please cite both this software and the
  mumax3 framework it visualizes (see the references below).
title: >-
  MumaxVR: Real-time virtual-reality visualization for micromagnetic simulations
abstract: >-
  MumaxVR is a Unity/OpenXR front end for the mumax3 GPU micromagnetic solver.
  It renders each finite-difference cell as a GPU-instanced arrow inside a
  stereoscopic VR rig, from either saved OVF files or a live stream produced by
  a bundled Go sidecar that embeds the mumax3 engine. A physics-based filter,
  distance level-of-detail, and a grabbable box/lens/slice region-of-interest
  tool keep dense volumes readable.
